  "question": {
    "text": "Two point charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;having masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively,&nbsp;are projected from the same point with the same velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> in the region of a uniform magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> such that the velocity makes an angle&nbsp;<math><mrow><mi>θ</mi> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;with the magnetic field. If we neglect the mutual interaction between the particles, the distance from the point of projection where they will meet again for the first time is",
