  "solution": {
    "text": "Both the charged particle will follow the helical path and the particles will meet at the intersection of the two helix such that the pitch of one helix will be the integral multiple of the pitch of the other helix.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">1</mn></msub><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">M</mtext></mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">QB</mtext></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msub><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">M</mtext></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">QB</mtext></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msub><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">M</mtext></mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">QB</mtext></mfrac></math><br /><br />They will meet again when the first particle completes two revolutions and the second particle completes one revolution so distance will be given as<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">d</mtext><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">v</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">cos</mtext><mi>θ</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">t</mtext><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">v</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">cos</mtext><mi>θ</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">.</mtext><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">M</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">QB</mtext></mfrac><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">Mv</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">cos</mtext><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">QB</mtext></mfrac></math>",
